meta {
  name: Update Step - Evidence Materials
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

put {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngPersonId/incidents/:id/steps/evidence-materials
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  youngPersonId: 1
  id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  evidence_materials: CCTV footage from common room (14:15-15:00) - saved to incident folder. Photographs of damaged TV remote control. Written statements from two staff members present. YP's daily log entry from that day.
  evidences[0][id]: 5
  evidences[0][description]: Updated description for existing evidence
  evidences[0][evidence_type]: photo
  delete_evidence_ids[0]: 3
  delete_evidence_ids[1]: 4
}

docs {
  # Update Step: Evidence / Supporting Materials
  
  This endpoint updates evidence records and the general evidence materials text field.
  
  ## Request Body Fields:
  
  ### 1. `evidence_materials` (string, optional)
  Text field for listing evidence collected. Common evidence types:
  - CCTV footage
  - Photographs  
  - Written statements
  - Medical reports
  - Damaged items
  - Documents
  
  ### 2. `evidences` (array, optional)
  Update metadata for existing evidence records:
  ```json
  {
    "evidences": [
      {
        "id": 5,
        "description": "Updated description",
        "evidence_type": "photo"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ### 3. `delete_evidence_ids` (array of integers, optional)
  Delete evidence records by ID. Files will also be removed from storage:
  ```json
  {
    "delete_evidence_ids": [3, 4, 7]
  }
  ```
  
  ## Evidence Types:
  - photo
  - video
  - document
  - audio
  - other
  
  ## Response:
  Returns the updated incident with `evidences` relationship loaded, showing all evidence records with their metadata.
  
  ## HOW TO UPLOAD FILES:
  
  **DO NOT use this endpoint to upload files!**
  
  Use the dedicated evidence upload endpoint instead:
  
  ### Upload New Evidence File:
  ```
  POST /v1/house/{house}/young-persons/{youngPersonId}/incidents/{id}/evidences
  Content-Type: multipart/form-data
  
  file: [your file]
  evidence_type: photo
  description: Photo of injury
  ```
  
  ### Other Evidence Endpoints:
  - `GET /incidents/{id}/evidences` - Get all evidence files
  - `PUT /incidents/{id}/evidences/{evidenceId}` - Update evidence metadata
  - `DELETE /incidents/{id}/evidences/{evidenceId}` - Delete evidence
  - `GET /incidents/{id}/evidences/{evidenceId}/download` - Download evidence file
  
  ### Legacy Attachment Endpoints (Deprecated):
  - `POST /incidents/{id}/attachments` - Upload attachment
  - `DELETE /incidents/{id}/attachments/{attachmentId}` - Delete attachment
  - `GET /incidents/{id}/attachments/{attachmentId}/download` - Download attachment
}
